UPDATE companies SET description='Arkansas Steel Associates, LLC (ASA) was founded in 1989 as a joint venture between Yamato Kogyo and Sumitomo Corporation. The plant is located in northeast Arkansas in the town of Newport on 300 acres.

ASA manufactures merchant bar quality (MBQ) billets, hot-rolled double-shoulder railroad tie plates, and hot-rolled flat bars in various cross sections and lengths. The company operates on a 300-acre site in Newport and is described as the producer of railroad tie plates in North America. Its tie plates accommodate rail sizes from 115RE to 140RE and meet AREMA and customer specifications; all products meet Buy America requirements.

The company serves customers ranging from small contractors to Class 1 railroads, supplying tie plates and flat bars for railroad infrastructure projects. Its products are used in North American rail networks and meet Buy America provisions for federally funded projects.

ASA emphasizes quality and environmental management, holding ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14001:2015 certifications, as well as AAR M-1003 and GSCC-SBET certifications. The company has published a decarbonization plan targeting zero Scope 2 emissions from its electric furnaces.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015','AAR M-1003','GSCC-SBET']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MBQ billet production", "Hot-rolled tie plate manufacturing", "Hot-rolled flat bar manufacturing", "AREMA specification compliance", "Customer specification compliance", "Buy America compliance", "Quality management (ISO 9001:2015)", "Environmental management (ISO 14001:2015)"], "industries": ["Railroad", "Construction", "Steel manufacturing"], "materials": ["Steel", "Merchant bar quality (MBQ) steel", "Hot-rolled steel"], "equipment": ["Electric furnaces"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Leading producer of railroad tie plates in North America", "All products meet Buy America requirements", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14001:2015 certified", "AAR M-1003 certified", "Decarbonization plan targeting zero Scope 2 emissions from electric furnaces"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 as joint venture between Yamato Kogyo and Sumitomo Corporation -> /", "Plant located in Newport, Arkansas on 300 acres -> /", "Leading producer of railroad tie plates in North America -> /", "Produces MBQ billets, hot-rolled tie plates, hot-rolled flat bars -> /", "Tie plates accommodate rail sizes 115RE to 140RE, meet AREMA and customer specs -> /", "All products meet Buy America requirements -> /", "Customer base ranges from small contractors to Class 1 railroads -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "ISO 14001:2015 certified -> /", "AAR M-1003 certified -> /", "GSCC-SBET certified -> /", "Decarbonization plan targeting zero Scope 2 emissions from electric furnaces -> /", "Founded year 1989 -> db", "Certifications ISO9001, ISO14001 -> db", "Headquarters Newport, Arkansas -> db"], "