UPDATE companies SET description='Auto Parts Company operates from three Missouri locations: its headquarters in Moscow Mills, just outside the St. Louis metropolitan area, plus yards in Joplin on Highway 43 and St. James on I-44 between St. Louis and Springfield. The company has been in business for decades, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The company specializes in late-model salvage, dismantling foreign and domestic cars, light trucks, and vans. It sells recycled and aftermarket parts, offers rebuilder services, and also retails late-model vehicles. Customers can order parts online by make, model, part number, or VIN. The operation ships nationwide via UPS or common carrier and provides free delivery to a wide corridor of cities across Missouri, Arkansas, and Oklahoma. A 90-day warranty covers all parts sold.

Its free-delivery zone spans St. Louis, Hannibal, Quincy, Columbia, Jefferson City, Rolla, Springfield, Joplin, Branson, Fayetteville, Tulsa, and Bentonville, indicating a regional focus with national reach.

