UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1988 in Chesapeake, Virginia, BBG Incorporated began as an engineering firm focused on electronic design and manufacturing for commercial and military sectors.

Today BBG provides end-to-end solutions that span hardware and software design, PCB layout and fabrication, data conversion, firmware development, and full product assembly. Its in-house production line handles everything from small-batch prototypes to high-volume runs, supported by automated testing, visual inspection systems, and scalable assembly processes that include wire harnessing and mechanical enclosure integration. The firm also fields shipboard installation and integration teams for U.S. and foreign naval platforms.

The company serves defense, aerospace, and commercial markets, counting prime contractors such as Northrop Grumman, BAE Systems, Lockheed Martin, and General Dynamics among its long-term partners. Its ruggedized Ethernet products, test equipment, and custom electronics are deployed in mission-critical ground, air, and maritime systems, including shipboard installations for U.S. and allied navies.

BBG emphasizes its ability to modernize legacy systems while integrating cutting-edge technology, citing seamless transitions between old and new hardware as a core differentiator. The firm attributes its on-time delivery record to vertical integration of design, test, and manufacturing under one roof, a model it says reduces lead times and design risk.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Design & Fabrication", "PCB Manufacturing", "PCB Testing", "Data Conversion", "Software Engineering", "Firmware Development", "RTOS Implementation", "HMI/GUI Design", "FPGA/CPLD Engineering", "Product Design & Development", "Product Assembly", "Wire Harnessing", "System Integration", "Shipboard Installation", "Shipboard Services", "System Modernization", "Quality Control", "Automated Testing", "Visual Inspection", "Legacy System Modernization", "Embedded Systems Development", "Networking & Wireless Protocols"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Military", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["USA-made manufacturing solutions", "End-to-end in-house production from prototype to high volume", "Automated testing and visual inspection systems", "Expertise in U.S. and foreign military shipboard integration", "Legacy-to-modern system conversion"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> /about", "Headquarters in Chesapeake, Virginia -> db", "Provides end-to-end solutions including hardware/software design, PCB fabrication, data conversion, firmware, product assembly -> /about, /capabilities", "In-house production from small-batch prototypes to high-volume runs -> /about, /capabilities", "Automated testing and visual inspection systems -> /about", "Shipboard installation and integration for U.S. and foreign naval platforms -> /capabilities", "Serves defense, aerospace, commercial markets -> /about, /capabilities, /", "Prime contractor partners: N