UPDATE companies SET description='BIG SIN WOOD was founded in 2018 by Jeremy Morrow in New York. Morrow, originally from Nashville, Tennessee, established the shop in Katonah, New York, though most projects are delivered and installed throughout New York City. The business began after Morrow left a career as a professional bass trombonist, bringing a musician’s discipline to woodworking.

The company produces custom furniture, fixtures, and installations on a commissioned basis, handling each project from design through fabrication, finishing, delivery, and installation. Work is built to order in their Katonah shop, with an emphasis on hand-selected lumber and the option to incorporate locally sourced or reclaimed wood. No facility size or headcount figures are published.

Morrow states that controlling every step—design, build, finish, delivery, and install—ensures quality and a personal connection to the material. The approach reflects his belief that knowing the origin of the wood, whether it’s white oak, plywood, or reclaimed stock, adds meaning to the finished piece.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture fabrication", "Fixture fabrication", "Architectural installation", "Design-build services", "Material selection and sourcing", "Reclaimed wood processing"], "industries": [], "materials": ["White oak", "Plywood", "Reclaimed wood", "Locally sourced wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-point responsibility: design, build, finish, delivery, and installation by the same person", "Hand-selected lumber for each project", "Option to use locally sourced or reclaimed wood", "Founder\u2019s background in professional music informs craftsmanship discipline"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2018 by Jeremy Morrow -> /about", "Founder from Nashville, TN, lives/works in New York -> /about", "Shop located in Katonah, NY -> /about", "Most work delivered to New York City -> /about", "Custom furniture, fixtures, installations built-to-order -> /", "Commissioned-based works from design to build -> /", "Hand-selected materials, locally recycled/reclaimed wood -> /about", "White oak and plywood mentioned as materials -> /about", "Founder background as professional bass trombonist -> /about", "Single-person design through installation philosophy -> /about", "Headquarters Brooklyn, NY per database -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom furniture, fixtures, and installations built-to-order in new york.", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='big-sin-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BK Industries operates in Meridian, Idaho, serving the Treasure Valley. The shop is owned and operated by Brian Krah, a lifelong motorsports enthusiast with nearly 20 years of professional automotive experience. Before establishing BK Industries, Krah owned and operated an automotive repair and performance shop in eastern Idaho and worked as a Honda technician at a dealership, building deep expertise with Japanese vehicles.

The facility provides automotive service, maintenance, and performance upgrades. Its work spans routine repairs, scheduled maintenance, and performance tuning for a range of vehicles. While the shop specializes in Japanese makes, it also services domestic and other import brands.

The customer base consists of vehicle owners in the Treasure Valley seeking repair, maintenance, or performance enhancements. The shop’s Japanese-car focus draws enthusiasts of brands such as Honda, while its broader experience accommodates domestic and other import models.

