UPDATE companies SET description='BTL Liners operates from an 84,000-square-foot fabrication facility in Prineville, Oregon. The company traces its roots to 1981 when Ron Perlatti founded Bend Tarp & Liner in nearby Bend, initially installing pond liners before partnering with a Japanese firm to develop heavyweight reinforced polyethylene liners. Ownership passed to Perlatti''s son Brad and his wife Jan in 1997, and in 2021 their daughter Chelsea and her husband Travis Wilcox took over, marking the third generation of family leadership.

The company manufactures custom geomembrane liners, covers, and tarps using reinforced polyethylene (RPE), reinforced polypropylene (RPP), and low-density polyethylene (LDPE). Its Prineville plant houses welding and fabrication equipment capable of producing single panels up to 150,000 square feet, supported by a team of 20-plus technicians. BTL also provides installation assistance worldwide, either onsite or remotely.

BTL serves agriculture, aquaponics, energy, golf courses, greenhouses, irrigation, landfill, mining, and water-feature markets. Project examples include cable wake-board parks in California and Ohio, a 40-acre irrigation reservoir in the western U.S., frac-tank insulated covers, a coal mine in British Columbia, and custom truck and boat tarps shipped globally.

The business began after Perlatti identified a need for a stronger, lighter alternative to HDPE, PVC, and EPDM liners. The resulting double-scrim RPE material can be prefabricated and installed quickly, offering a cost-effective solution. BTL''s stated mission is to give clients confidence that its containment systems exceed requirements for resource conservation and control.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom geomembrane fabrication", "Welding of reinforced polyethylene and polypropylene", "Prefabrication of large panels up to 150,000 sq ft", "Installation assistance (onsite and remote)", "Design of containment systems", "Fabrication of tarps and covers"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Aquaponics", "Energy", "Golf courses", "Greenhouse", "Hydroponics", "Irrigation", "Landfill", "Mining", "Water features", "Frac tanks", "Truck and boat tarps", "Ice skating", "Wake board parks"], "materials": ["Reinforced polyethylene (RPE)", "Reinforced polypropylene (RPP)", "Low density polyethylene (LDPE)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest single panels in the industry at 150,000 square feet", "Installation assistance worldwide, onsite or over the phone", "45 years in business since 1981", "Over 280 years of combined industry experience", "Third-generation family-owned business"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 by Ron Perlatti -> /about-us", "Third generation family-owned -> /about-us", "Facility 84,000 sq ft since 2007 -> /about-us", "Employees 20+ -> /about-us", "Materials: RPE, RPP, LDPE -> /about-us", "Largest single panels 150,000 sq ft -> /", "Installation assistance worldwide -> /", "Industries served: agriculture, aquaponics, energy, etc. -> /", "Projects: cable wake board parks, golf courses, etc. -> /", "Mission: provide confidence and peace of mind -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "BTL Liners has designed, fabricated and constructed the most durable, dependable custom geosynthetic systems on the planet.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "20+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='btl-liners' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BY DESIGN Furniture & Interior Design operates from a showroom in Clive, Iowa, a suburb of Des Moines. The business traces its roots to December 1976 when Russell and Ruthann Clark helped their son Kevin and daughter-in-law Bonita open Wood Stock Ltd., a store dedicated to unfinished wood furniture in Des Moines. The current BY DESIGN entity was established in 1998 after the Clarks merged their wood specialty store with an upholstery concept called Sofas by Design.

The firm combines a retail showroom with a full-service interior design studio. Its designers — degreed professionals — help clients specify customizable furniture sourced from vendors such as American Leather, Four Hands, Norwalk Furniture, and BDI. The showroom features a fabric wall stocked with thousands of fabrics and leathers, and dining tables can be ordered in wood, tile, stone, or glass tops with various finishes. The company also offers furniture restoration services and a furniture protection plan.

BY DESIGN serves residential clients throughout the Des Moines metro area and also partners with outside designers through a to-the-trade program. Its customer base includes homeowners furnishing living rooms, dining rooms, bedrooms, home offices, and outdoor spaces. The company’s portfolio includes projects ranging from single-room refreshes to whole-home designs.

The Clarks founded the business on a mission to listen, inform, and inspire clients who view their homes as a focal point of their lives. The company emphasizes that it does not impose a signature style but instead helps each client discover a personal aesthetic through highly customizable product options and one-on-one design consultation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Interior design consultation", "Custom furniture specification", "Space planning", "Furniture restoration", "Furniture protection plans", "To-the-trade design services"], "industries": ["Residential interior design", "Home furnishings retail", "To-the-trade design services"], "materials": ["Fabric", "Leather", "Wood", "Tile", "Stone", "Glass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Degreed interior designers on staff", "Fabric wall with thousands of fabrics and leathers", "Customizable furniture from multiple vendor lines", "Furniture protection program covering entire purchase", "To-the-trade program for outside designers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998, lineage to 1976 Wood Stock Ltd. -> /about-us", "Founders Russell and Ruthann Clark, Kevin and Bonita Clark -> /about-us", "Family-owned, locally owned small business -> /about-us, /", "Headquarters Clive, Iowa -> db, /", "Degreed designers, customizable furniture from vendors (American Leather, Four Hands, Norwalk, BDI) -> /, /about-us", "Fabric wall with thousands of fabrics/leathers -> /about-us", "Furniture restoration, protection program -> /, /about-us", "To-the-trade program for outside designers -> /about-us", "Mission: listen, inform, inspire, no signature style -> /about-us", "Showroom at 1490 NW 86th St, Clive, IA 50325 -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "As a locally owned small business, we take pride in providing personalized interior design services from our degreed designers, along with customizable, high-quality furnitu