UPDATE companies SET description='Bald Ridge Enterprises operates from Cody, Wyoming, where it was founded nearly four decades ago as a small local shop built on family values. The company is registered as a Women-Owned Small Business with the U.S. federal government and has grown into a regional contractor serving Wyoming and Montana.

The company provides complete metal construction services, specializing in architectural sheet metal fabrication and installation. Its in-house shop produces pre-manufactured steel buildings, metal roofing systems, siding, soffits, fascia, gutters, downspouts, and specialty items such as snow bars, chimney caps, and custom planter boxes. A carpentry division adds wood detailing to projects. All components are designed, fabricated, and installed by the company''s own crews, giving it control over quality from start to finish.

Bald Ridge serves commercial, agricultural, residential, institutional, and government customers across the two-state area. Projects range from personal shops and farm structures to large-scale institutional and government facilities. The company''s online design tool allows clients to configure building layouts and request quotes remotely.

The firm differentiates itself by building to the Architectural Sheet Metal Manual, the industry''s highest standard, and by engineering its systems for the extreme weather of Wyoming and Montana. It backs its work with a standard one-year warranty plus extended manufacturer guarantees, and emphasizes a family-focused culture that has retained a certified, insured team for nearly 40 years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural sheet metal fabrication", "Pre-manufactured steel building fabrication", "Metal roofing system fabrication and installation", "Metal siding, soffits, fascia, gutters, downspouts fabrication and installation", "Specialty metalwork (snow bars, chimney caps, custom planter boxes)", "Carpentry", "Design and engineering", "In-house fabrication", "Installation"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Agricultural construction", "Residential construction", "Institutional construction", "Government construction"], "materials": ["Steel", "Sheet metal", "Metal roofing panels", "Metal siding panels"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house fabrication for complete quality control", "Builds to the Architectural Sheet Metal Manual, the industry''s highest standard", "Engineered for Wyoming and Montana''s extreme weather conditions", "Certified, insured team with nearly 40 years of experience", "Standard 1-year warranty with extended manufacturer guarantees"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Cody, Wyoming -> db", "Founded nearly four decades ago -> /about-us", "Women-Owned Small Business with US Federal Contractor Registration -> /about-us", "In-house fabrication of all components -> /, /about-us", "Services: pre-manufactured steel buildings, metal roofing, metal siding, specialty metalwork, carpentry -> /services", "Industries served: commercial, agricultural, residential, institutional, government -> /about-us, /services", "Team of 16 named employees -> /about-us", "Builds to Architectural Sheet Metal Manual -> /, /about-us", "Standard 1-year warranty with extended manufacturer guarantees -> /", "Online building design tool -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every element is designed and fabricated in-house to meet the highest industry standards.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bald-ridge-enterprises-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ballard Sheet Metal Works Inc. has operated from Seattle, Washington, since 1907. The family-owned and operated business began over a century ago on Ballard Avenue Northwest, serving the Greater Puget Sound area with custom metal fabrication.

The shop provides a wide range of fabrication services, including flashing, backsplashes, corner guards, sill pans, thresholds, countertops with integrated sinks, custom sinks, hoods, fireplace surrounds, barbecues, planter boxes, railings, stairs, awnings, and chimney caps. It also handles marine projects such as fire dampers, custom HVAC components, welding, and tanks. Shearing capacity runs from 24‑gauge material up to 3/8‑inch steel sheet at 10‑foot lengths, and the company works with galvanized steel, hot‑ and cold‑rolled steel, aluminum, prepainted steel, stainless steel, copper, zinc, Cor‑Ten, brass, and diamond plate. Certified welders perform both shop and field welding, and field measurement and installation are available.

Customers include local contractors, architects, and residential homeowners across the Puget Sound region. The company’s marine work serves the maritime industry, while its HVAC and architectural metalwork support commercial and residential construction. Reviews highlight projects for homeowners needing custom countertops, fireplace surrounds, and boat repairs.

The firm emphasizes its team’s experience and the ability to handle projects of any size, from small residential jobs to large commercial contracts. Its long history and in‑house fabrication and installation capabilities are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['Contractor License BALLASM134CR','Certified welders']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding (shop & field)", "Field measurement", "Installation", "Flashing fabrication", "Backsplash fabrication", "Corner guard fabrication", "Sill pan fabrication", "Threshold fabrication", "Countertop fabrication", "Custom sink fabrication", "Custom hood fabrication", "Fireplace surround fabrication", "Custom barbecue fabrication", "Planter box fabrication", "Railing fabrication", "Stair fabrication", "Awning fabrication", "Chimney cap fabrication", "Marine fabrication (fire dampers, custom HVAC, tanks)", "Shearing (up to 3/8\" steel x 10ft)", "Material shearing to size"], "industries": ["Construction", "Residential", "Marine", "HVAC", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Hot-rolled steel", "Cold-rolled steel", "Aluminum", "Prepainted steel", "Stainless steel", "Copper", "Zinc", "A606 (Cor-Ten)", "Brass", "Tread (diamond) plate"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1907", "Certified welders for shop and field welding", "Shearing capacity: 24 gauge to 3/8\u2033 steel at 10 ft", "Handles projects of all sizes for contractors, architects, and homeowners", "In-house fabrication, field measurement, and installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1907, family-owned, Seattle WA -> db", "Custom metal fabrication, welding, field measure/installation -> /", "Product list: flashing, backsplashes, corner guards, sill pans, thresholds, countertops, custom sinks, hoods, fireplace surrounds, barbecues, planter boxes, railings, stairs, awnings, chimney caps, marine work (fire dampers, custom HVAC, welding, tanks) -> /", "Shearing capabilities: min 24 gauge x 12 ft, max 3/8\" steel x 10 ft -> /", "Materials: galvanized, hot/cold rolled steel, aluminum, prepainted steel, stainless steel, copper, zinc, A606 (Cor-Ten), brass, tread plate -> /", "Certified welders for shop & field welding -> /", "Serves local contractors, architects, customers (residential and commercial) -> /", "Contractor License BALLASM134CR -> /", "Reviews indicate residential and marine customers -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Quality Custom Metal Fabrication, Welding and Field Measure and/or Installation Services Available in the Greater Puget Sound Area", "founded_year": "1907", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ballard-sheet-metal-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Barbett Industries Inc. operates from Reading, Pennsylvania, where it manufactures narrow fabrics. The company is led by President Frank J. Loos and his son, General Manager Joseph Loos, indicating a family-run operation.

The firm produces a broad line of custom and commodity narrow fabrics, including braids, cords, and trims such as twist cord, draw cord, lamp shade trim, Chinese braid, bolo cord, industrial braid, metallic braid, jacquard braids, and various fringes. Finishing processes encompass custom dyeing, acetate tipping, hot and cold cutting, metal barbing, cord and tassel assembly, textile crimping, and waxing. The manufacturing shop is located in the United States, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Barbett serves apparel manufacturers, producers of braided vinyl and leather goods, fishing lure makers, flag component suppliers, home furnishings companies, industrial clients, and military uniform trim contractors. The company also replicates customer samples and provides production cost estimates, and accepts customer-supplied goods for finishing work.

