UPDATE companies SET description='Barn XO operates from Mundelein, Illinois, where the family-owned business reclaims rare Midwestern woods originally harvested during Chicago''s industrial rise in the late 1800s and early 1900s. The company was founded on the premise of preserving the history embedded in each knot, grain, and imperfection of this reclaimed lumber.

The workshop produces custom handcrafted furniture including conference tables, bar and dining tables, chairs and bar stools, desks, console tables, and coffee tables. Each piece is built to order through a process that begins with a design consultation, continues with material and finish selection at the company''s showroom, and ends with nationwide delivery.

Barn XO serves both residential and commercial clients. Homeowners order dining tables, benches, and coffee tables for private residences, while businesses specify conference tables for offices and bar-height tables for hospitality venues.

The brand differentiates itself by emphasizing sustainable design that honors the origins of its materials. Barn XO states that its furniture carries the history of Chicago''s industrial past, and it markets its products as made in the USA with free design consultations and a showroom experience in Mundelein.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Reclaimed wood sourcing", "Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted furniture manufacturing", "Finish selection and application", "Nationwide shipping", "Design consultation", "Showroom visits"], "industries": ["Commercial office furniture", "Residential furniture", "Hospitality furniture"], "materials": ["Reclaimed Midwestern woods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated", "Reclaims rare Midwestern woods from Chicago''s late 1800s/early 1900s industrial era", "Custom handcrafted furniture made in the USA", "Ships nationwide with free design consultation", "Showroom in Mundelein, IL for material and finish selection"], "facts_used": ["Location: Mundelein, Illinois -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Reclaims Midwestern woods from late 1800s/early 1900s Chicago -> /", "Custom handcrafted furniture: conference tables, dining tables, chairs, desks, etc. -> /", "Design consultation and showroom process -> /", "Ships nationwide -> /", "Made in USA -> /", "Serves residential and commercial customers -> /", "Sustainable design emphasis -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom. Handcrafted. Family-Owned.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='barn-xo' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Barrett Petfood is headquartered in Brainerd, Minnesota. The company was founded in 2006 when agricultural entrepreneur Mike Barrett purchased a piece of equipment intended for agricultural manufacturing, only to discover it was suited for food production. Mike and his children, Tom and Sarah Barrett, pivoted the business into pet food, with Mike later transitioning ownership to his children while continuing to supply ingredients from his farm. The company remains family-owned.

Barrett operates two facilities in central Minnesota: the original Brainerd plant and a second site opened in 2020 in Little Falls that added 160,000 square feet and two production lines. The company produces hundreds of formulas across super‑premium kibble, kibble‑plus, and freeze‑dried formats, using extrusion, milling, and automated packaging lines. Its capabilities span diet formulation, ingredient sourcing, processing, packaging, and distribution.

Barrett serves pet food brands ranging from emerging labels to market leaders, manufacturing diets for dogs, cats, reptiles, birds, livestock, and zoo animals. Customers rely on the company as a full‑service co‑manufacturer that handles everything from formulation to shipping.

The business was built on a simple promise: “If we wouldn’t feed it to our own pets, you won’t find it in our products.” The Barretts emphasize a relationship‑based philosophy, a “Don’t Say No” innovation mindset, and rigorous, laboratory‑like food‑safety standards as their differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion", "Freeze-dried processing", "Milling", "Diet formulation", "Ingredient sourcing", "Automated packaging", "Labeling", "Distribution", "Quality assurance (laboratory-like standards)", "Supply chain management", "Co-manufacturing", "Brand services"], "industries": ["Pet food manufacturing", "Super premium kibble", "Kibble plus", "Animal feed (livestock, zoo animals)", "Pet food brands (emerging to market leaders)"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Extrusion lines", "Freeze-drying equipment", "Automated packaging lines", "Industry-specific processing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, nimble execution with continuous innovation", "Relationship-based philosophy prioritizing integrity, transparency, and partnership", "\u201cDon\u2019t Say No\u201d philosophy enabling innovation on complex diets", "Clean, modern facilities with rigorous laboratory-like food safety standards", "Full-service partnership from diet formulation through distribution"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Brainerd, Minnesota -> db", "Founded in 2006 by Mike Barrett -> /about", "Family-owned, Tom and Sarah Barrett took over leadership -> /about", "Pivot from agricultural equipment to pet food -> /about", "Second facility in Little Falls opened 2020, 160,000 sq ft, two production lines -> /about", "Produces hundreds of formulas for dogs, cats, reptiles, birds, livestock, zoo animals -> /about", "Processes: extrusion, freeze-dried, milling, automated packaging -> /, /services", "Capabilities: diet formulation, ingredient sourcing, processing, packaging, distribution -> /, /services, /about",