UPDATE companies SET description='Barth Electronics, Inc. has been headquartered in Boulder City, Nevada since 1976, when the company relocated from Ohio to support weapons testing at the Nevada Test Site. Founded in 1964, the firm began by designing and manufacturing specialized test hardware for EG&G in Las Vegas and for national laboratories.

The company designs and manufactures sub-nanosecond high-energy pulse power instrumentation, including over 100 distinct pulse power products. In 1997 its engineers developed the first commercial Transmission Line Pulser (TLP) for the electrostatic discharge (ESD) industry. Today the product line encompasses the Model 4002 TLP+ for human-body-model testing, the Model 4012 VFTLP+ for charged-device-model testing, the Model 4702 HMM+ for IEC-equivalent gun discharge testing, and a 700-series of 3 kV and 5 kV pulse generators. All ESD testing services are performed in-house at the Boulder City factory, and a rental program is offered for the Model 4002 TLP+.

Barth serves the semiconductor industry with ESD device characterization and qualification testing, while its pulse power instruments are used daily in physics and pulse-power laboratories worldwide. Historical customers include EG&G and U.S. national laboratories involved in weapons testing.

The company traces its high-reliability standards to its weapons-testing heritage: “By beating our swords into plowshares, weapons testing hardware was changed into the development and manufacture of the highest quality ESD test equipment available today.” It continues to investigate new technologies for ESD and high-voltage pulse power as needs emerge.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pulse power instrumentation design and manufacturing", "ESD test equipment manufacturing (TLP, VFTLP, HMM)", "ESD device testing services (Human Body Model, Charged Device Model, IEC gun discharge)", "High voltage pulse generator manufacturing (3 kV, 5 kV)", "Test equipment rental program", "Sub-nanosecond high energy pulse measurement"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Physics research", "Pulse power laboratories", "Defense/weapons testing", "National laboratories"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Model 4002 TLP+", "Model 4012 VFTLP+", "Model 4702 HMM+", "700 series pulse generators (3 kV and 5 kV)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First commercial Transmission Line Pulser (TLP) for ESD industry (1997)", "All ESD testing performed in-house at Boulder City factory, nothing outsourced", "Over 100 pulse power product variants available", "Rental program for Model 4002 TLP+ pulse curve tracer", "High-reliability heritage from weapons testing at Nevada Test Site"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Boulder City, Nevada since 1976 -> /about", "Founded in 1964 -> /about", "Originated in Ohio, moved to support Nevada Test Site weapons testing -> /about", "Designed test hardware for EG&G and national laboratories -> /about", "Developed first commercial TLP for ESD industry in 1997 -> /about", "Over 100 pulse power products -> /about", "Product models: 4002 TLP+, 4012 VFTLP+, 4702 HMM+, 700 series pulse generators -> /about, /services", "ESD testing services performed in-house at Boulder City factory -> /services", "Rental program for Model 4002 TLP+ -> /services", "Serves semiconductor industry, physics and pulse power laboratories -> /about", "Historical customers: EG&G, national laboratories -> /about", "High-reliability heritage from weapons testing -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializing in designing and manufacturing ''state of the art'' sub-nanosecond high energy, pulse power instrumentation since 1964", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='barth-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Base Power Company was founded in 2023 in Austin, Texas, by CEO Zach Dell and co-founder Justin Lopas. Lopas previously led manufacturing at Anduril and worked on rockets at SpaceX, while the broader team brings experience from satellite constellation launches and early electric vehicle production. The company was born after Winter Storm Uri left millions of Texans without power for days, highlighting the grid’s fragility and rising electricity costs.

The company handles battery pack assembly, in-house engineering, UL-certified testing, and runs a virtual power plant that dispatches stored energy to the grid during peak demand.

The primary customers are residential homeowners in Texas and Illinois seeking affordable backup power and fixed-rate electricity. The company also serves grid-storage and utility markets by aggregating its distributed batteries to provide grid-balancing services. Testimonials cite installations in Houston, Waxahachie, Cypress, Arlington, Saginaw, and Pflugerville.

Base positions its model as a low-cost alternative to traditional generators or solar-plus-storage, installing the battery for a $695 one-time fee plus a $19 monthly membership, with an all-in energy rate around 13.9¢/kWh. The battery is tested for -22°F to 122°F and submersion-rated to three feet, and the company says it earns revenue from grid services rather than marking up energy, allowing it to keep rates low.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 1973','UL 1741','UL 9540','UL 9540A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["battery pack assembly", "in-house engineered battery systems", "UL certified testing", "virtual power plant / grid services operation", "retail electric provider", "home battery backup deployment", "grid-balancing battery network hardware"], "industries": ["residential", "grid storage", "utility"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["39.2 kWh whole-home battery (one of the largest available)", "Backup installed for $695 versus ~$13,000 for a traditional generator", "Fixed all-in electricity rate of 13.9\u00a2/kWh guaranteed at renewal", "Battery participates in grid balancing to lower customer rates", "Tested for -22\u00b0F to 122\u00b0F and submersion-rated to 3 feet"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2023 -> db", "Headquarters Austin, Texas -> db", "CEO Zach Dell, co-founder Justin Lopas -> /about-us", "Designs, assembles, deploys home battery backup systems -> db description", "Operates as retail electric provider in Texas -> db description", "30,000+ homes across Texas and Illinois -> /", "39.2 kWh Core battery -> /", "Backup duration 36-72 hours -> /", "Operating temperature -22 to 122\u00b0F, submersion-rated to 3 feet -> /", "Installation fee $695, membership $19/mo, energy rate 13.9\u00a2/kWh -> /", "Certifications UL 1973, UL 1741, UL 9540, UL 9540A -> db", "Capabilities: battery pack assembly, in-house engineered battery systems, UL certified testing, virtual power plant/grid services operatio