UPDATE companies SET description='Belmont Medical Technologies is headquartered in Billerica, Massachusetts. The company was founded in 1980 by Dr. George Herzlinger as Belmont Instrument Corporation, initially developing simulation EKG equipment and cardiac assist devices.

The company designs and manufactures fluid warming and temperature regulation systems for critical care. Its product line includes the Belmont® Rapid Infuser RI‑2 for high‑speed, bubble‑free blood and fluid delivery; the buddy lite® portable fluid warmer; the BloodNav™ MTP documentation tool; the Burn Navigator® for evidence‑based burn resuscitation; the Allon® and CritiCool® non‑invasive temperature management systems; and the Hyperthermia Pump™ for cavity lavage. Belmont employs nearly 200 people and has expanded its manufacturing and office facility in 2019 and again in 2022.

Belmont’s devices are used in hospital operating rooms, intensive care units, emergency departments, labor and delivery suites, and on military combat fields and emergency transport vehicles worldwide. The U.S. military awarded the company a five‑year contract worth up to $133 million in 2020, and group purchasing agreements are in place with Inc. and HealthTrust. The company also donated rapid infusers and portable warmers to Ukraine in 2022.

Belmont states that its differentiation lies in blending technical inspiration with an uncompromising quality standard, earning the trust of clinicians through patented electromagnetic heating technology, aluminum‑free disposables, and automatic air detection and removal features. The company holds MDSAP certification for its quality system and maintains direct operations in the United Kingdom and Germany.', certifications=ARRAY['MDSAP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fluid warming", "Temperature regulation", "Hyperthermic lavage", "Rapid infusion", "Portable fluid warming", "MTP performance improvement and automatic documentation", "Evidence-based fluid management for burns", "Non-invasive patient temperature management", "Electromagnetic induction warming", "Automatic air detection and removal", "Real-time monitoring and graphical display", "EMR integration", "Aluminum-free disposable manufacturing", "Battery and AC powered device design", "Close-to-patient warming"], "industries": ["Medical facilities", "Military", "Emergency transport", "Anesthesia", "Surgical care", "Trauma and emergency", "Labor and delivery", "Intensive care"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented electromagnetic heating technology", "Aluminum-free disposables across product lines", "Military tested and approved (buddy lite)", "MDSAP certified quality system", "Direct operations in the UK and Germany"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Billerica, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded 1980 by Dr. Herzlinger -> /about-us", "Founder George Herzlinger -> /about-us", "Acquired by Audax Private Equity 2017 -> /about-us", "Product lines: Rapid Infuser RI-2, buddy lite, BloodNav, Burn Navigator, Allon, CritiCool, Hyperthermia Pump -> /, /about-us", "Nearly 200 employees -> /about-us", "Manufacturing facility expansion 2019, 2022 -> /about-us", "MDSAP certification 2018 -> /about-us", "U.S. Military contract up to $133M 2020 -> /about-us