UPDATE companies SET description='Bixby Electric Inc. operates from its headquarters and yard in Albuquerque, New Mexico, serving a six-state region that includes Colorado, Texas, Arizona, California, and Wyoming. The company has been in business for over 40 years and describes its culture as family-oriented, though no founding year or individual founders are disclosed publicly.

The firm provides electrical construction, testing, and service across commercial, industrial, and infrastructure projects. Core capabilities include airfield lighting and NAVAID installation and maintenance, traffic signalization, roadway and high-mast lighting, intelligent transportation systems, weigh-in-motion systems, directional boring and vertical drilling, vacuum excavation, and transmission and distribution work up to 115 kV. Bixby also offers infrared thermography, ultrasonic testing, arc-flash studies, power-quality analysis, commissioning, and rental of a 2002 Sterling LT9500 vac truck and a 2011 International 4300 Elgin sweeper truck, both operated by Bixby crews.

Customers range from private developers to state and local agencies. The company has worked on water and wastewater treatment plants, healthcare facilities, manufacturing sites, solar installations, and mining operations where its technicians hold MSHA certifications. Public-sector references include the Bear Canyon Pedestrian Bridge lighting and the Montaño Rail Runner station projects in New Mexico.

Bixby emphasizes a "what we install, we maintain" philosophy backed by two dedicated service departments—one for electrical and one for transportation systems. The firm runs a four-year apprenticeship program through the Northern New Mexico Independent Electrical Contractors Association and maintains memberships in NMUCA, ABC New Mexico, and ACNM.', certifications=ARRAY['MSHA certification (for mine and pit work)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical construction", "Electrical testing (infrared thermography, ultrasonic, power quality, arc flash studies)", "Electrical service and maintenance", "Airfield lighting and NAVAID installation and maintenance", "Traffic signalization and roadway lighting", "Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS)", "Weigh In Motion (WIM) systems", "Horizontal directional drilling", "Vertical drilling (pressure digger up to 54\" diameter, 20'' deep)", "Vacuum excavation / potholing", "Transmission and distribution up to 115 kV (underground and overhead)", "Medium voltage installations", "Lighting retrofits", "Solar energy installations", "Water and wastewater electrical installations", "Healthcare facility electrical construction", "Commercial and industrial electrical construction", "Residential electrical service", "Vac truck rental (hydro-excavation)", "Sweeper truck rental", "Commissioning services", "Emergency repair services"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Industrial construction", "Infrastructure", "Transportation (airfield, roadway)", "Government / public sector", "Healthcare", "Water and wastewater treatment", "Mining", "Solar energy", "Utilities", "Sports lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Sterling LT9500 Vac Truck (2002)", "International 4300 Elgin Sweeper Truck (2011)", "Pressure digger (up to 54\" diameter, 20'' deep)", "Directional boring equipment (two crews)", "Vacuum excavation equipment", "Infrared thermography equipment", "Ultrasonic measurement tools", "Voltage, current, and power qualit