UPDATE companies SET description='Blount Fine Foods operates from Warren, Rhode Island, where the company has been rooted since 1880. Eddie B. Blount founded an oyster business on the coast of West Barrington, and the enterprise passed through five generations of the Blount family. In the 1940s, F. Nelson Blount shifted the focus to a clam operation in Warren, and Ted Blount later diversified into value‑added seafood items such as clam chowder during the 1980s. Today the business remains family‑owned and operated, led by the sixth generation.

The company manufactures premium fresh prepared foods — soups, chowders, mac & cheese, sides and entrees — using kettle‑cooking methods and modern facilities. A large production plant in Fall River, Massachusetts supports volume manufacturing, and the product line is distributed to grocery stores, club stores and restaurants across all 50 states. Blount also runs a food‑service and hot‑to‑go division that produces private‑label items for national brands.

Customers include retail grocery chains, warehouse clubs, food‑service operators and restaurant groups.

